[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760239174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104628#issuecomment-2760239174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104628","id":2760239174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6khehG","user":{"login":"EricEzaM","id":41730826,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzMwODI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41730826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM","html_url":"https://github.com/EricEzaM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T05:35:00Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T05:35:55Z","body":"> Additionally, there's an issue where the 2D editor will take priority over the shortcut, so it doesn't work if you are currently in the 2D editor viewport (even though it'll work on selected 2D nodes if you're in the 3D editor viewport). It seems EditorNode::shortcut_input() isn't called anymore as soon as the 2D editor viewport is focused.\r\n\r\nShortcut is already used and being consumed by this menu in the 2d editor:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e9137e7-129e-4278-8147-d90f45910c7e)\r\n\r\nI wrote in the godot rocketchat about this, but I'll put it here if its easier for more people to see/find if its useful.\r\n\r\nI wish there was a better way of debugging shortcut issues like this, but there isn't as far as I know. Here are the steps I use to find the root cause of such issues.\r\n\r\n1. Add code to scene_tree.cpp so you can conditionally put a breakpoint and suspend execution when the key combination you want is pressed (some IDEs support conditional breakpoints but they are very slow). This MUST be within a condition because this method is called for every input (including mouse move)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df12fa49-6b0f-4b88-bfaf-2ea29ef71482)\r\n2. Run Godot with debugger attached\r\n3. Press the key combination to activate the shortcut in the scenario when it does not work\r\n4. Breakpoint gets hit, execution is suspended\r\n5. Enable a breakpoint in control.cpp `accept_event`\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa67c5ad-2501-42ec-9c8d-7f4f335b790c)\r\n6. Resume execution\r\n7. `accept_event` breakpoint is hit. Look at the call stack and see which control accepted the event.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fae8d78a-f2b5-4ac5-9b0e-33c2a6acb328)\r\n\r\nOnly enable the breakpoint in accept_event after the scene_tree breakpoint is hit, otherwise this will be triggered constantly. Note some IDEs allow for setting breakpoints to be dependent on hitting another one first:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e44c73af-7f30-4bcd-b501-2085c003219f)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760239174/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2762233842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104628#issuecomment-2762233842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104628","id":2762233842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kpFfy","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T19:21:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T19:21:10Z","body":"@EricEzaM Thanks for the help! I've changed Show Helpers in the 2D editor to <kbd>Shift + H</kbd> to avoid conflicts with the new shortcut. (We can't use <kbd>Ctrl + H</kbd> as its macOS counterpart <kbd>Cmd + H</kbd> is reserved by the OS.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2762233842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3923627196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104628#issuecomment-3923627196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104628","id":3923627196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7p3cy8","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github